# Knowledge Health Score

Spec: KnowledgeHealth
Purpose:
  Define per-node knowledge health score (0-100), the signal breakdown
  that feeds it, the Knowledge Graph Health report, and the Architecture
  Health report. Health is distinct from lifecycle status: a node can be
  ACTIVE with low health, signaling it needs review.

Owns: lifecycle/health-score.sdd

## Health Score Formula

  health (0-100) = weighted combination of signals:

  Signals:
    usage:
      weight: 0.30
      metric: number of references in active tasks/decisions in last 30 days
      +++ : 20+ references (score: 30)
      ++   : 5-19 references  (score: 20)
      +    : 1-4 references   (score: 10)
      0    : no references    (score: 0)

    evidence:
      weight: 0.25
      metric: number of independent evidence sources (code, tests, tasks, decisions)
      +++ : 5+ evidence sources (score: 25)
      ++   : 2-4 evidence sources (score: 17)
      +    : 1 evidence source     (score: 9)
      0    : no evidence          (score: 0)

    failures:
      weight: -0.15 (negative)
      metric: number of failed applications or contradicting evidence
      0 failures     (score: 0, no penalty)
      1-2 failures   (score: -10)
      3+ failures    (score: -15, cap)

    age:
      weight: 0.10
      metric: time since last review/validation
      < 30 days     (score: 10)
      30-180 days   (score: 5)
      180+ days     (score: 2)
      [DECAY-01] Age alone does NOT determine poor health.

    conflicts:
      weight: -0.10 (negative)
      metric: number of conflicts_with edges
      0 conflicts  (score: 0)
      1 conflict   (score: -10)
      2+ conflicts (score: -10, cap)

  health = usage_score + evidence_score + failures_score + age_score + conflicts_score

  Clamped to [0, 100].

## Health vs Status Distinction

  A knowledge node has BOTH a lifecycle status AND a health score:

  status: ACTIVE, health: 94
    → healthy, no action needed

  status: ACTIVE, health: 42
    → active but unhealthy — needs review
    → AI should propose: re-validate evidence, re-test, or deprecate

  status: STALE, health: 87
    → stale but well-evidenced — keep in index, monitor

  [HEALTH-01] Health score is recomputed daily by @agent.knowledge-cleaner.
  [HEALTH-02] Nodes with health < 50 AND status ACTIVE MUST be flagged for review.
  [HEALTH-03] Nodes with health < 30 AND status STALE are proposed for archival.
  [HEALTH-04] Health score is separate from trust level and confidence.
  [HEALTH-05] Human can override health score with explanation.

## Example Health Breakdown

  @skill.idempotency
    health: 94

    signals:
      usage:       +++  (referenced in 20+ tasks)
      evidence:    +++  (5 evidence sources: code, tests, tasks, decisions, production)
      failures:    -    (0 failures)
      age:         +    (last reviewed 15 days ago)
      conflicts:   0    (no conflicts)

  @skill.old-retry-pattern
    health: 42

    signals:
      usage:       0    (no references in last 6 months)
      evidence:    +    (1 evidence source: old code)
      failures:    -    (2 failed applications)
      age:         +    (last reviewed 200 days ago)
      conflicts:   1    (conflicts with @skill.retry-with-backoff)

## Knowledge Graph Health Report

  Periodic self-report produced by @agent.knowledge-cleaner:

  @health.report.GH-2026-09-01

  References:
    142 total
    87 established
    31 validated
    19 candidate
    5 deprecated
    0 conflicts

  Skills:
    50 total
    42 active
    5 stale
    3 deprecated

  Concepts:
    183 total
    161 active
    12 dormant
    10 deprecated

  Decisions:
    34 total
    30 active
    4 superseded

  Orphans:
    12 (no incoming references, >30 days old)

  Stale:
    7 (not referenced in 30+ days)

  Contradictions:
    1 (conflicts-with edge detected)

  Overall: HEALTHY

  Thresholds:
    HEALTHY  — health_score >= 0.7, conflicts = 0
    WEAK     — 0.4 <= health_score < 0.7, conflicts <= 2
    CRITICAL — health_score < 0.4, conflicts > 2

    AI behavior:
      HEALTHY  — proceed, reuse established references
      WEAK     — propose candidate promotion, flag gaps
      CRITICAL — pause and escalate to human review

## Architecture Health

  Same mechanism applied to architecture entities:

  @architecture.ddd
    used:
      14 domains (referenced across 14 bounded contexts)

    violations:
      3 (domain → infrastructure boundaries crossed)

    drift:
      medium

    unused:
      1 bounded context (no code implements it)

    health:
      87

  [ARCH-01] Architecture health is recomputed weekly.
  [ARCH-02] Violations with no accepted exception MUST trigger
            @exception.* proposal.
  [ARCH-03] Unused bounded contexts with health < 30 are candidates for
            archival.

